Comparison Layout: Prime Move Lens vs. Neutral Analysis (Random Sequence)

You have run the same random sequence (20 numbers) through 8 AI models under two conditions:

1. Lens condition – using the Prime Move structural lens with explicit instruction to return null if no structure.
2. Neutral condition – using a generic “describe any patterns” prompt without the five‑stage framework.

Below is a structured comparison across key dimensions.

---

1. Output Format

Aspect Lens (Prime Move) Neutral (generic)
Structure Rigid, five‑stage template (Split, Tension, Failed Merge, Scar, Decay) Free text, no fixed categories
Null expression Explicit “None” or “N/A” for each stage Varies: “no pattern”, “random”, “a‑structural”, “no meaningful persistent structure”
Length Very short (1–2 lines) Paragraph (several sentences)
Repeats / coincidences Ignored (not mentioned) Some AIs note that 96 and 5 repeat, but correctly dismiss them as coincidental

